namespace Erdos694

/-
# Problem Description

Erdős Problem 694. `erdos_694` is proved unconditionally here: the Linnik-type input
previously assumed in this repository as `linnik_dvd` is no longer needed.

The formalisation is by plby (github.com/plby/lean-proofs),
`src/latest/ErdosProblems/Erdos694.lean`, whose lower bound replaces the assumed Linnik-type
input by a uniform prime-counting theorem; that in turn rests on the Bombieri–Vinogradov theorem from
the `BoundedGaps` library of frenzymath/FormalPantheon.

Flattened single-file vendoring of the combined 293-module import closure (272 from
`BoundedGaps`, 21 from plby), in dependency order, with project-internal imports removed
so that `Mathlib` is the only import. Declarations keep their upstream fully-qualified
names, so modules that declare at the Lean root are emitted with an explicit `_root_.`
prefix. Twenty-five names are declared in more than one upstream module — legal there
because each has a `private`, and so module-scoped, declarer, and because no module
imports two declarers — and are disambiguated here with `_v1`/`_v2`/... suffixes,
rewritten consistently in each module that sees them. One further name, `R`, is public in
both declarers: it is the totient-ratio extremal function of the final statement in
plby's `Erdos694`, and the prime-counting error term `Psi x - x` in `BoundedGaps`. The
former keeps the name, so that `erdos_694` reads exactly as upstream; the latter is
renamed `psiError`. No mathematical content is changed.
-/


